# InvestigatAI API Development Standards

## API Route Structure
Every API route must follow this pattern:

```typescript
// app/api/investigations/route.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { withAuth, withSecurityHeaders, withRateLimit } from "@/lib/middleware/auth";
import { InvestigationService } from "@/core/investigation/services/investigation-service";
import { CreateInvestigationSchema } from "@/core/investigation/schemas/investigation-schemas";
import { auditEvents } from "@/core/security/audit/audit-service";

export const POST = withSecurityHeaders(
  withRateLimit(10, 15 * 60 * 1000)(
    withAuth(async (request: AuthenticatedRequest) => {
      try {
        // 1. Validate input
        const body = await request.json();
        const validatedData = CreateInvestigationSchema.parse(body);
        
        // 2. Business logic via core service
        const investigation = await InvestigationService.create(
          validatedData,
          request.user.id
        );
        
        // 3. Audit logging
        await auditEvents.investigationCreated(investigation.id, {
          name: investigation.name,
          userId: request.user.id
        });
        
        // 4. Return response
        return NextResponse.json({ data: investigation }, { status: 201 });
      } catch (error) {
        return handleAPIError(error);
      }
    })
  )
);
```

## Core Service Layer Pattern
All business logic must be in core services:

```typescript
// core/investigation/services/investigation-service.ts
import { Investigation } from "../entities/investigation";
import { InvestigationRepository } from "../repositories/investigation-repository";
import { UserAuthorizationService } from "@/core/security/auth/authorization-service";

export class InvestigationService {
  static async create(
    data: CreateInvestigationData,
    userId: string
  ): Promise<Investigation> {
    // 1. Authorization check
    await UserAuthorizationService.canCreateInvestigation(userId);
    
    // 2. Business validation
    this.validateInvestigationData(data);
    
    // 3. Domain object creation
    const investigation = Investigation.create({
      ...data,
      createdBy: userId,
      status: 'draft'
    });
    
    // 4. Persistence
    return await InvestigationRepository.save(investigation);
  }
  
  private static validateInvestigationData(data: CreateInvestigationData): void {
    // Business validation logic
  }
}
```

## API Standards

### 1. Input Validation
- Always use Zod schemas for validation
- Validate at API boundary, not in core services
- Sanitize user inputs
- Check file types and sizes for uploads

### 2. Error Handling
```typescript
// core/shared/errors/api-errors.ts
export class APIError extends Error {
  constructor(
    public code: string,
    public status: number,
    message: string,
    public details?: any
  ) {
    super(message);
  }
}

export const handleAPIError = (error: unknown): NextResponse => {
  if (error instanceof APIError) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: error.message, code: error.code, details: error.details },
      { status: error.status }
    );
  }
  
  if (error instanceof ZodError) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: "Validation failed", code: "VALIDATION_ERROR", details: error.errors },
      { status: 400 }
    );
  }
  
  // Log unexpected errors
  console.error("Unexpected API error:", error);
  return NextResponse.json(
    { error: "Internal server error", code: "INTERNAL_ERROR" },
    { status: 500 }
  );
};
```

### 3. Response Format
Standardize all API responses:

```typescript
// Success responses
{
  "data": T,
  "pagination"?: PaginationInfo,
  "meta"?: Record<string, any>
}

// Error responses
{
  "error": string,
  "code": string,
  "details"?: any
}
```

### 4. Authentication & Authorization
- Every protected route must use `withAuth` middleware
- Implement role-based access control
- Validate user permissions for specific resources
- Use JWT tokens with proper validation

### 5. Rate Limiting
- Apply appropriate rate limits per endpoint
- Different limits for different user roles
- Consider endpoint sensitivity for limits

### 6. Security Headers
- Always use `withSecurityHeaders` middleware
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Set CSP headers appropriately
- Use HTTPS-only cookies

## API Documentation
- Document all endpoints with JSDoc comments
- Include request/response examples
- Document error codes and meanings
- Maintain OpenAPI/Swagger spec

## Testing Standards
- Unit tests for all core services
- Integration tests for API routes
- Mock external dependencies
- Test error scenarios
- Test security boundaries